# Design & public presentation

This site represents an author / creator brand. First impressions matter (e.g. book launch). Aim for calm confidence, not startup-template energy.

## Brand & hierarchy

- **Brand first:** "Sarkany Nexus" should read as the hero signal on marketing surfaces; headlines must not overpower the brand
- **One job per section:** one purpose, one headline, short supporting copy
- **Hero budget:** brand, one line of promise, optional single CTA — no stat strips, chip clusters, or promo clutter in the first viewport
- Prefer full-bleed or atmospheric backgrounds over flat single-color slabs

## Look & feel

- Define and reuse CSS variables; extend `:root` in `assets/style.css`
- Avoid AI-default looks: purple-on-white gradients, generic Inter-only UI chrome, terracotta-on-cream, dense "newspaper" grids, glow spam, emoji decoration
- Prefer distinctive typography over default system/Inter-only stacks when redesigning
- Cards: only when they aid scanning a list of works; never card-ify the hero
- Motion: 2–3 intentional touches max; no noisy animation

## Quality bar

- Desktop and mobile both must feel finished
- Images: compress; prefer WebP/JPEG over huge PNGs; always set meaningful `alt`
- Coming-soon mode must still look intentional (not an unfinished scaffold)
- Copy: specific and human — avoid "Blooming", "Welcome to my website", lorem, filler
